WEBVTT

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.841
Good evening, and welcome to Nordic Crypto.

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:14.790
This is issue number two, with the Nordic crypto news from
the 5th to the 12th of October, 2026.

00:00:15.398 --> 00:00:19.221
Tonight: proposals in the Storting to pause new data
centres.

00:00:19.221 --> 00:00:23.585
Sweden's financial watchdog names thirty more suspected
fraud firms.

00:00:23.585 --> 00:00:27.413
And new EU anti-money-laundering standards that touch
crypto.

00:00:30.018 --> 00:00:35.772
The Red Party has proposed in the Storting a temporary halt
for new data centres, with a licensing regime.

00:00:35.772 --> 00:00:40.191
It argues that crypto-mining data centres get power ahead of
local industry.

00:00:40.191 --> 00:00:42.870
None of the proposals singles out crypto.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.745
That's from Stortinget.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:50.898
Socialist Left Party members have also proposed a pause on
new data centres and a national licensing system, and ask

00:00:50.898 --> 00:00:55.490
the government to report on how the Storting's call for a
crypto-mining ban will be followed up.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:58.012
This is a proposal, not a decision.

00:00:58.618 --> 00:01:04.577
In Ságat, the data-centre company Arctic Core says it uses
crypto mining to earn income during a test phase, but argues

00:01:04.577 --> 00:01:08.133
this does not change the character of the building it has a
permit for.

00:01:08.742 --> 00:01:14.996
Finansavisen reports that customers of the Norwegian
exchange Firi bought 16.1 million kroner more crypto than

00:01:14.996 --> 00:01:16.304
they sold in September.

00:01:16.304 --> 00:01:18.368
Bitcoin was the top buy.

00:01:18.962 --> 00:01:25.529
Kaupr reports that Ace Digital, listed on Euronext Growth
Oslo, made an unaudited third-quarter net profit of 6.3

00:01:25.529 --> 00:01:28.086
million kroner, and says it now has no debt.

00:01:30.702 --> 00:01:37.304
Nyheter24 reports that Finansinspektionen has warned against
thirty more firms operating without a licence, some offering

00:01:37.304 --> 00:01:38.286
trading in crypto.

00:01:38.286 --> 00:01:41.813
That brings this year's warnings to 227.

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:47.988
And Finansinspektionen reports that the EU's
anti-money-laundering authority, AMLA, has sent three draft

00:01:47.988 --> 00:01:50.498
technical standards to the European Commission.

00:01:50.498 --> 00:01:55.565
They include rules for crypto-asset service providers, and
still need the Commission's adoption.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.386
That's all for issue number two.

00:01:58.386 --> 00:02:03.107
Every story, with a link to the original source, is at
nordiccrypto.no.

00:02:03.107 --> 00:02:05.753
Nothing here is investment advice.

00:02:05.753 --> 00:02:09.290
From all of us: good night, from the Nordic Crypto team.

